  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual of the Black man as the perpetrator",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the Black man (person), interpreting him as the subject of the violent act described in the text. The menacing expression and the racialized visual are used to imply the user (or the viewer) is identifying with or projecting the role of the criminal perpetrator onto this figure. This projection is reinforced by the text 'i raped that mexican hard', which uses first-person pronouns ('i') to directly involve the viewer in the act, making the user the implied perpetrator. The visual material (person) is the entity onto which the user is projected, as the user sees themselves as the one who committed the crime described.",
